notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T04:19:18.690Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence 2026-07-27: the reported critical path is not a work sequence, it is a duplicate cluster.\n\npm graph analyze returns execution.critical_path as pm-phpq, pm-204c, pm-iziy, pm-f0e9, pm-mn6w, pm-wjdr, pm-a5ea. Reading those seven items shows what the chain actually is. They are titled Release-readiness maintenance loop 2026-03-07 run 2, run 3, and so on: a set of near-identical items produced by a repeating maintenance loop on a single day in March 2026. Their own history records the relationship explicitly. Each of the trailing six carries a comment written on 2026-04-04 by a dedupe pass reading, verbatim, that this item is superseded by pm-phpq for cluster release-loop::2026-03-07.\n\nSo the longest path the analyzer can find through this workspace is six hops of duplicate consolidation. The edges that carry it are related edges, all created at one instant on 2026-07-26 by the terminal-history backfill, which is exactly the right thing for that backfill to have recorded and exactly the wrong thing to present as a critical path. The analytic is not wrong about the graph; the graph does not contain a longer chain of anything else.\n\nTwo consequences worth separating.\n\nThe first is that the depth deficit this item describes is worse than the raw number suggests. A critical path of six sounds shallow; a critical path of six that turns out to be one item and five copies of it means the true longest sequence of causally ordered work in a two-thousand-item corpus spanning months is shorter than six. There is no ordered spine at all, only a wide flat rim and one hub.\n\nThe second is a concrete remediation that costs nothing to justify, because the evidence is machine-written and unambiguous. Those duplicate-consolidation relationships are supersedes, not related. Retyping them removes fabricated ordering signal from the execution DAG at the same time as it makes the consolidation lineage traversable, so it improves both halves of the problem with one change and no judgement call. A first tranche of this was applied on 2026-07-27 under the evidence rules in pm-lnrk: 39 supersedes edges recovered from durable text, taking the kind from 1 edge to 40 across the corpus. The remaining work is not more extraction, it is deciding whether the analyzer should treat related as an ordering edge at all, which is the question this item and pm-4020c5 meet on."
body: ""
